 "prompt_text": "[gMASK]<sop><|user|>A tank holds 1,200 litres. Pipe A fills it in 40 minutes and pipe B in 60 minutes, while a drain empties a full tank in 120 minutes. All three are opened together on an empty tank. How long until it is full? Show the working.<|assistant|><think></think>",
 "completion_text": "# Setting Up the Problem\n\n**Work rates (tank per minute):**\n- Pipe A fills: 1/40 of the tank per minute\n- Pipe B fills: 1/60 of the tank per minute\n- Drain empties: 1/120 of the tank per minute\n\n**Combined rate:**\n\n$$\\frac{1}{40} + \\frac{1}{60} - \\frac{1}{120}$$\n\nUsing a common denominator of 120:\n\n$$\\frac{3}{120} + \\frac{2}{120} - \\frac{1}{120} = \\frac{4}{120} = \\frac{1}{30}$$\n\nSo together they fill **1/30 of the tank per minute**.\n\n# Solving for Time\n\n$$\\text{Time} = \\frac{1 \\text{ tank}}{1/30 \\text{ tank per minute}} = 30 \\text{ minutes}$$\n\n# Check (using litres)\n\n- Pipe A: 1200 \u00f7 40 = 30 L/min\n- Pipe B: 1200 \u00f7 60 = 20 L/min\n- Drain: 1200 \u00f7 120 = 10 L/min\n\nNet rate: 30 + 20 \u2212 10 = **40 L/min**\n\nTime to fill 1200 L: 1200 \u00f7 40 = **30 minutes** \u2713",
